Z||000002||Alex4mula||02-02-2000||03:32 PM||||Mine is a Formula V6 stick. I know when my TPS is going bad because in the cold morning when I drive away accelerating in 1st in low RPMs the car stumbles a little bit. Gets worst with time and no code is generated. I replace TPS and feels like a new car and I can slam the pedal without stumbling. In worst cases (wet non-GM TPS after cleaning engine) it just gave a code.||||reg||1
